<p align="left" class="body1"><span class="body1 style73"> <h2>News archive</h2><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-02-27 | Tuesday</font></strong><br/><br/><img alt="Archived image unavailable" height="185" width="246"><br>Ryan
O'Neill, 19, visits with his girlfriend, Anna Vinokurova, also 19, in
her room at the Seattle Medical and Rehabilitation Center in Seattle
last week. Vinokurova was seriously injured several months ago when she
was struck by a car on her way to class at Edmonds Community College. Photo: <strong><em>Dan Bates / <a class="massline-external-gap" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20090315005756/http://heraldnet.com/stories/07/02/26/100loc_a1support001.cfm" rel="noopener noreferrer">The Herald</a><br><br/></br></em></strong><font size="2">Student <em>Anna Vinokurova</em>, 19, has been hospitalized with
brain damage since Oct. 24, 2006 when she was struck by a car while
crossing 68th Ave. W. on her way to class<br>
<br><strong>
Edmonds Community College</strong> students have organized a benefit to help pay
medical bills for a fellow student injured in a pedestrian accident.<br>
<br><em>
Dizzlepalooza</em>, a music benefit with 10 bands and dance teams including
headliners the hip-hop duo<strong> Common Market</strong>, Northwest rock band The
Classic Crime and Jamaican singer Lexie Lee, will be 7 p.m., March 2 in
Seaview Gym.<br>
<br>
Student Ronnie “Dizzle” Morrison, the student government representative
for diversity, will also perform with his hip-hop group D203. The
students decided to turn a planned music festival into a benefit after
Vinokurova’s hospitalization of more than three months. She was taking
classes at the college with plans to transfer to a four-year university
to study to become a veterinarian.<br>
<br>
Students hope to attract as many as 750 people to the event. <strong>The cost
will be $5 for Edmonds Community College and Central Washington
University-Lynnwood students, $10 for the public.</strong><br>
<br>
Tickets can be purchased on campus in the college bookstore or online
at <a class="massline-external-gap" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20090315005756/http://masslinemedia.com/news/www.edcc.edu/boxoffice" rel="noopener noreferrer">www.edcc.edu/boxoffice</a>. For more information, call the Office of
Student Life at 425-640-1581.</br></br></br></br></br></br></br></br></br></br></font><p></p><br/><hr align="center" noshade="" size="1" width="400"/><br/><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-02-26 | Monday</font></strong><br/><br/><strong>"Why I Hate Blacks"</strong><br>(from <em>Asian Week</em> Feb. 23 - Mar. 1, 2007, Vol. 27 No. 27)<br>by <em>Kenneth Eng</em><br><br>Here is a list of reasons why we should discriminate against blacks, starting from the most obvious down to the least obvious.<br><br>*Blacks hate us. Every Asian who has ever come across them knows that they take almost every opportunity to hurl racist remarks at us. In my experience, I would say about 90 percent of blacks I have met, regardless of age or environment, poke fun at the very sight of an Asian. Furthermore, their activity in the media proves their hatred: Rush Hour, Exit Wounds, Hot 97, etc.<br><br>*Contrary to media depictions, I would argue that blacks are weak-willed. They are the only race that has been enslaved for 300 years. It's unbelievable that it took them<br>that long to fight back. On the other hand, we slaughtered the Russians in the Japanese-Russo War.<br><br>*Blacks are easy to coerce. This is proven by the fact that so many of them, including Reverend Al Sharpton, tend to be Christians. Yet, at the same time, they spend much of their time whining about how much they hate "the whites that oppressed them." Correct me if I'm wrong, but wasn't Christianity the religion that the whites forced upon them?<br><br>Blacks don't get it. I know it's a blunt and crass comment, but it's true. When I was in high school, I recall a class debate in which one half of the class was chosen to defend black slavery and the other half was chosen to defend liberation. Disturbingly, blacks on the prior side viciously defended slavery as well as Christianity. they say if you don't study history, you're condemned to repeat it. In high school, I only remember one black student ever attending any of my honors and AP courses. And that student was caught cheating.<br><br>It is rather troubling that they are treated as heroes, but then again, whites will do anything to defend them.<br><br/>- - -<br/><br/>Kenneth, who wears a New Era Ass Hat size 8 1/2, must now answer to Asian American communities nationwide about his racist and irresponsible so-called journalism.<br/><br/>Former Asian Week editor-in-chief Neela Banerjee responds to Eng's op-ed <a class="massline-external-gap" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20090315005756/http://hyphenmagazine.com/blog/archives/2007/02/asianweek_takes.html" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>here</strong></a>. <br/><br/>You can also read/sign the online petition <a class="massline-external-gap" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20090315005756/http://ipetitions.com/petition/asianweek/" rel="noopener noreferrer">here</a>.<br/><br/>What are your thoughts on this? Post them up on the forums now! <a href="/bluescholars/massline-forums/index.html">Please sign up</a> and let's have some healthy dialogue.<br/><br/>Peace<br/>dj daps1<p></p><br/><hr align="center" noshade="" size="1" width="400"/><br/><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-02-23 | Friday</font></strong><br/><br/>Happy Friday, y'all -- I need everyone and their mother's uncle's dentist to head out to the brand spankin' new <strong><a class="massline-external-gap" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20090315005756/http://theveraproject.org/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Vera Project</a></strong> at Seattle Center to catch special performances of our fam <strong>Grayskul</strong>, <strong>Youth Movement Records</strong>, <strong>Khingz of Ab Creole</strong>, and <strong>Massline</strong> artists <strong>Common Market</strong>. By the looks of the pic above it appears that <strong>RA Scion</strong> of Common Market is ready. And plus, the show is like $free.99! Show info on your right, sis-ham.<br><br>Follow the bouncing <strong>Sabzi</strong> as he will <a class="massline-external-gap" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20090315005756/http://farm1.static.flickr.com/177/396204092_4e5dcfe62d.jpg" rel="noopener noreferrer">make an appearance at Hidmo</a> after the Vera Project show, then behind the tables at <strong>Gabriel Teodros</strong>' "<em>Lovework</em>" album release party with <strong>DJ WD4D</strong> the following night.<br><br>Have a filthy weekend!<br/>Peace<br/>dj daps1<p></p><br/><hr align="center" noshade="" size="1" width="400"/><br/><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-02-23 | Friday</font></strong><br/><br/><img alt="Archived image unavailable" height="200" width="200"><br><br>VS<br><br><img alt="Archived image unavailable" height="200" width="200"><br/><br/>VS<br/><br/><img alt="" height="149" src="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/assets/f701e34c155041a6c99e.jpg" width="200"><br/><br/>Rick Ross - Hustlin' Remix feat. Jay-Z and Young Jeezy | <a class="massline-external-gap" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20090315005756/http://sendspace.com/file/d367le" rel="noopener noreferrer">mp3</a><br/>Immortal Technique - Watch Out | <a class="massline-external-gap" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20090315005756/http://sendspace.com/file/y5cbbx" rel="noopener noreferrer">mp3</a><br/>Khingz (of Ab Creole) - Fucc Wit Ya | <a class="massline-external-gap" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20090315005756/http://sendspace.com/file/ex76lf" rel="noopener noreferrer">mp3</a><br/><br/>Peace<br/>dj daps1<p></p><br/><hr align="center" noshade="" size="1" width="400"/><br/><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-02-22 | Thursday</font></strong><br/><br/><img align="middle" alt="Archived image unavailable" height="768" width="298"><br><br>1976: Brothers Johnson - Tomorrow (prod. by <strong>Quincy Jones</strong>) | <a class="massline-external-gap" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20090315005756/http://sendspace.com/file/w7zf0a" rel="noopener noreferrer">mp3</a><br>1990: Quincy Jones feat. Tevin Campbell - Tomorrow | <a class="massline-external-gap" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20090315005756/http://sendspace.com/file/ctch33" rel="noopener noreferrer">mp3</a><br>1997: OC - Far From Yours (feat. Yvette Michelle) | <a class="massline-external-gap" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20090315005756/http://sendspace.com/file/xzu6sw" rel="noopener noreferrer">mp3</a><br/>2002: Blue Scholars - Sagaba | <a class="massline-external-gap" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20090315005756/http://sendspace.com/file/4ptc3f" rel="noopener noreferrer">mp3</a><br/><br/>Other connections? Megaproducer Quincy Jones grew up in <a class="massline-external-gap" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20090315005756/http://achievement.org/autodoc/photocredit/achievers/jon0-059" rel="noopener noreferrer">Bremerton</a>, hometown to Geologic of Blue Scholars.<br/><br/>Peace<br/>dj daps1<p></p><br/><hr align="center" noshade="" size="1" width="400"/><br/><center><div class="pagenumbers"><a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-b9d0c0fa332b.php">[&lt;&lt;]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-ff41e4b899bf.php">[1]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-f09e4ab70de0.php">[2]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-13fd6b501db4.php">[3]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-a6d8d32ad781.php">[4]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-d45f54b0cbc4.php">[5]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-0bfc403792bc.php">[6]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-fd78b8847920.php">[7]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-cd30dd4ecbb4.php">[8]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-3f0473af164e.php">[9]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-3